Author: kenziedadon <kenziedadon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Oct 1 07:13:41 2026 -0500

    WO1: fix HERE crash + Unscreenable rename
    
    Two blockers plus cleanups, reviewed and signed off 2026-10-01.
    
    Blockers:
    - token_grade.py: HERE was never defined, so TokenGrader() raised
      NameError on no-arg construction. That is the path taken by
      self_test(), the CLI, and every production caller (disco_run,
      trend_discovery, disco_post). The suite never caught it because
      every test passes journal_path explicitly, short-circuiting the
      `or`. WO1 fail-closed logic had never actually executed.
    - Unscreeable -> Unscreenable, 41 occurrences across 3 files: class
      names, the result dict key, the journal filename, and test names.
      Zero remaining.
    
    Also:
    - _is_superchain_token called but defined as _is_superchain (was
      silently eating -10 on the promotion path)
    - GABLE_PAUSABLE -> GATE_PAUSABLE
    - SUPERCHAIN_LIST_URL was the literal " "; now "", fails closed with
      no network call rather than a bogus URL
    - test hygiene: dead _grader_with_payload removed, unused
      urllib.request import, tempfile.mktemp -> tmp_path
    
    No logic changes beyond the above. 23 tests pass; TokenGrader()
    constructs; live WETH/USDC grade BLUECHIP.

