# ==== COMMIT e9d9314 (WO1 follow-up, 2026-10-03) ====
commit e9d93149a74e5e0ffb8d27827902fa8feee25e8b
Author: kenziedadon <kenziedadon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 3 05:06:53 2026 -0500

    WO1: fix HERE crash, Unscreenable rename, GABLE_PAUSABLE typo,
    correct SUPERCHAIN_LIST_URL rationale
    
    Four changes, all in token_grade.py.
    
    1. HERE crash fix (the original scope). HERE was referenced at the
       journal path construction but never defined, so _journal_rejection
       raised NameError before writing. Now defined at module level.
    
    2. Unscreenable spelling rename, complete. Unscreeable* -> Unscreenable*
       across import, exception catch, result dict key, and two raise sites.
       GATE_UNSCREENABLE / GRADE_UNSCREENABLE were already correct.
       Journal file unscreeable.jsonl -> unscreenable.jsonl (no pre-existing
       file: the HERE crash meant no journal could have been written under
       either name).
    
    3. GABLE_PAUSABLE -> GATE_PAUSABLE, previously undisclosed. Pre-fix this
       raised NameError on any token with is_pausable=True, caught by the
       outer except Exception, so those tokens got no verdict at all rather
       than a pausable rejection. Fix restores the gate.
    
    4. SUPERCHAIN_LIST_URL rationale corrected, previously undisclosed.
       " " -> "" is a BEHAVIORAL NO-OP: both raise ValueError in
       urllib.request.Request, both swallowed by the except Exception: pass
       in _is_superchain(), both return False, neither makes a network call.
       The prior comment claimed a -10 promotion-path penalty via a "broad
       market-check handler". That mechanism does not exist in this code
       path. Comment now states the actual behavior. Code value unchanged.

